{
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "description": "Single-screen Teleport status board. Designed for TV / ops huddle. Big numbers, threshold colours, no scrolling.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "**Fraction of this namespace's scrape targets that are up.**\n\nThe denominator is the PEAK target count seen over the retention window, not a hand-maintained number. That matters for two reasons:\n\n- `avg(up)` cannot detect a target that *vanishes*. Scale a Deployment to zero and its series disappears entirely, so the average of the survivors stays at 1.0 and the tile reads a confident 100% while something is gone.\n- A hardcoded expected count goes stale the moment anyone adds a scrape target. This panel briefly read **114%** for exactly that reason: deploying the usage exporter took the namespace from 7 targets to 8 while the constant still said 7.\n\nUsing the observed peak fixes both. It is clamped to the CURRENT count because the subquery only samples hourly: without the clamp, a target added minutes ago is not yet in the peak and the tile reads over 100% until the next sample. That is how this panel was caught reading 112% moments after the exporter was deployed. A target that vanishes still counts against the denominator until it ages out, and a newly added target raises the peak on its own.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Deliberately removing a target holds this below 100% until the peak ages out of `$prom_retention`. That is the honest reading \u2014 the target really did go away \u2014 but expect it after a planned decommission.\n\nAnchored on `$namespace` rather than `$teleport_job`: the latter derives from `teleport_build_info`, which the Postgres exporter does not emit, so the target feeding the whole database row was outside this health check.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.9
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(up{namespace=~\"$namespace\"}) / clamp_min(max_over_time(count(up{namespace=~\"$namespace\"})[$prom_retention:1h]), scalar(count(up{namespace=~\"$namespace\"})))",
          "legendFormat": "Cluster Up",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Cluster Status",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "prometheus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Total resources (nodes, apps, kube clusters, databases) connected to the Teleport cluster. teleport_connected_resources is a PER-AUTH-INSTANCE gauge: every auth replica reports the whole cluster's inventory, so a plain sum() would multiply the count by the number of auth replicas. max by (type) collapses the replicas first, then sums the resource types \u2014 correct with 1 auth today and still correct under auth HA.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(max by (type)(teleport_connected_resources{namespace=~\"$namespace\",job=~\"$teleport_job\"}))",
          "legendFormat": "Connected Resources",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Connected Resources",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "prometheus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Active SSH sessions right now. DO NOT wrap this in rate() or increase(): despite the _total suffix, proxy_ssh_sessions_total is metadata-confirmed a GAUGE (\"Number of active sessions through this proxy\"), so using it bare is correct. SSH only \u2014 Kubernetes, database, app and desktop sessions are not counted here.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "purple",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(proxy_ssh_sessions_total{namespace=~\"$namespace\",job=~\"$teleport_job\"})",
          "legendFormat": "SSH Sessions",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Active SSH Sessions",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "prometheus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Worker nodes (kube_node_role role=\"node\") reporting Ready=true. Must be sum(), not count(): kube-state-metrics keeps emitting the status=\"true\" series at value 0 when a node goes NotReady, so count() never drops. Joined against kube_node_role so the control plane is excluded. Expected worker count is 1 \u2014 raise the green threshold if you scale the nodes instance group.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(kube_node_status_condition{condition=\"Ready\",status=\"true\"} * on(node) group_left kube_node_role{role=\"node\"})",
          "legendFormat": "Ready Workers",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Worker Nodes Ready",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "kubeStateMetrics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "${DS_TELEPORT_BACKEND}"
      },
      "description": "Successful user.login events in the audit log over the last 24h. Sourced from the audit backend, NOT from the Prometheus counter user_login_total, which over-reports by roughly 7x: it incremented +7 in a 45-minute window on 2026-08-27 against exactly one audit user.login event, because it also counts re-authentications and session refreshes. If you want a Prometheus-side activity signal instead, teleport_user_certificates_generated is trustworthy (7d increase 2023 vs 2023 cert.create audit events). Fixed 24h window, independent of the dashboard time range.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "${DS_TELEPORT_BACKEND}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT count(*) AS \"Logins (24h)\"\nFROM public.events\nWHERE event_type = 'user.login'\n  AND event_data->>'success' = 'true'\n  AND event_time >= now() - interval '24 hours'",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Logins Today (24h)",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "audit.postgres"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "${DS_TELEPORT_BACKEND}"
      },
      "description": "Failed user.login events in the audit log over the last 24h \u2014 covers SSO (oidc/saml/github), local password and web login failures. Red at 10. Sourced from the audit backend, NOT from the Prometheus counter failed_login_attempts_total, which cannot see most login failures: it is exported only by job=\"teleport\" (the proxies) and job=\"teleport/ssh-node\", never by teleport-auth where SSO and local logins are actually evaluated. It is the SSH-server-side failed-auth counter. Evidence: the audit log holds 27 failed logins all-time (16 oidc, 11 local) while max_over_time(failed_login_attempts_total[7d]) is 0 on every series \u2014 a permanently green tile for something it cannot measure. Fixed 24h window, independent of the dashboard time range.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "${DS_TELEPORT_BACKEND}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT count(*) AS \"Failed Logins (24h)\"\nFROM public.events\nWHERE event_type = 'user.login'\n  AND event_data->>'success' = 'false'\n  AND event_time >= now() - interval '24 hours'",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Failed Logins Today (24h)",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "audit.postgres"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Audit/S3 emit errors in the last 15 minutes. Anything > 0 is red. (Title, legend, description and the query window all say 15m \u2014 they previously disagreed: the title said 15m, the legend said 1h and the description said \"the last hour\" while the query was increase(...[15m]), so a reader trusting the description under-reacted by 4x.)",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(increase(audit_failed_emit_events{namespace=~\"$namespace\",job=~\"$teleport_job\"}[15m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Audit Errors (15m)",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Audit Upload Errors (15m)",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "prometheus"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "CPU usage (cores) of the BUSIEST teleport container \u2014 max over pods, not the average. The old avg() diluted a hot pod across 6 containers (avg 0.0027 cores while auth ran at 0.0062), and its 0.5/0.9 core thresholds were unreachable: one pod would have had to burn 3.0 cores to push the average past orange and 5.4 past red. Thresholds are now set against observed reality \u2014 the 7d per-pod peak is 0.036 cores (proxy), so orange at 0.1 is ~3x peak and red at 0.25 is half of the only CPU limit in the namespace (ssh-node, 500m; auth and the proxies have no limit, so \"cores\" here is not anchored to a budget). Gauge max is 0.5 so normal load is actually visible on the dial. Still scoped to container=\"teleport\" and deliberately not filtered by $teleport_job \u2014 cAdvisor metrics do not carry that label.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.25
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 0.5
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "id": 8,
      "options": {
        "minVizHeight": 75,
        "minVizWidth": 75,
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showThresholdLabels": false,
        "showThresholdMarkers": true,
        "sizing": "auto"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(max by (pod)(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace=~\"$namespace\",container=\"teleport\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "Busiest pod (cores)",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "CPU \u2014 Busiest Teleport Pod (cores)",
      "type": "gauge",
      "x-requires": [
        "kubeStateMetrics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "Memory working set of the HEAVIEST teleport container \u2014 max over pods, not the average. The old avg() read 62-77 MB and hid teleport-auth at 215 MB (~3x the average, since the proxies sit near 60 MB and the agents near 40 MB), and it carried no thresholds at all. Orange at 400 MB / red at 700 MB: ssh-node is the only container with a memory limit (512Mi), so red is set above it to catch a genuine runaway while orange fires before ssh-node would be OOMKilled. 7d per-pod peak is 215 MB (auth).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 400000000
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 700000000
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "decbytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "id": 9,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(max by (pod)(container_memory_working_set_bytes{namespace=~\"$namespace\",container=\"teleport\"}))",
          "legendFormat": "Heaviest pod",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Memory \u2014 Heaviest Teleport Pod",
      "type": "stat",
      "x-requires": [
        "kubeStateMetrics"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": [
    "teleport",
    "rev-tech"
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
